@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# 0001 — Reservation expiry is derived from the clock, not swept
+
+Status: accepted (2026-10-29)
+
+## Context
+Holds must lapse after their TTL, but the package has no background job and all time
+comes from the injected `Clock`.
+
+## Decision
+A hold is live iff its stored status is `ACTIVE` and `clock.now() < expires_at`.
+Every read that depends on holds (`reserved`, `available`, `reserve`, `place_order`)
+evaluates this against the clock. Reading a lapsed `ACTIVE` hold (`get_reservation`,
+`confirm_reservation`, `release_reservation`, idempotent `reserve`) persists it as
+`EXPIRED`. Only `ACTIVE` can become `EXPIRED`; `CONFIRMED`/`RELEASED` are final.
+
+## Consequences
+- No sweep API; correctness does not depend on anyone calling one.
+- Stored status may lag (`ACTIVE` past `expires_at`) — never trust the stored status alone;
+  go through the service. A future DB repository must filter live holds by `expires_at`.
+- Assumes the clock does not move backwards (as `FixedClock` enforces); otherwise an
+  `EXPIRED` hold would not revive.
diff --git a/docs/adr/0002-reservation-idempotency-keys.md b/docs/adr/0002-reservation-idempotency-keys.md
