index 0000000..8985b13
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0002-reservation-idempotency-keys.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# 0002 — Reservation idempotency keys are global and permanent
+
+Status: accepted (2026-10-29)
+
+## Context
+The cart service retries `reserve`; a retry must not hold stock twice.
+
+## Decision
+- One global key namespace (not per warehouse).
+- A key is bound to its first *successful* request: warehouse + requested items
+  (what was asked, not what a partial hold got; item order ignored).
+- Same key + same request → the existing reservation in its current state, even if
+  `CONFIRMED`, `RELEASED` or `EXPIRED`; `expires_at` is not moved. A key never creates a
+  second hold.
+- Same key + different request → `IdempotencyConflict`, whatever the original's state.
+- A failed `reserve` leaves no trace; its key stays free.
+
+## Consequences
+Keys are never freed, so the key store grows with every reservation. Pruning old keys
+would need its own decision.
