index 0000000..87f3417
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/stock-reservations.md
@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# Stock reservations (holds)
+
+## What and why
+
+Checkout needs to hold stock for a cart before payment, then either confirm the hold
+into an order or release it. Holds nobody confirms lapse on their own after a while.
+Retries from the cart service must be safe, so every `reserve` call carries an
+idempotency key.
+
+## Interface (fixed by the owner — verbatim)
+
+Interface — hidden tests call exactly this; `InventoryService(repository, ledger, clock)` keeps working as is:
+- `InventoryService.reserve(warehouse: str, items: dict[str, int], idempotency_key: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.confirm_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Order`
+- `InventoryService.release_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.get_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.available(sku, warehouse)` must take holds into account.
+- `inventory.models`: dataclass `Reservation` with `reservation_id: str`, `warehouse: str`, `items: dict[str, int]` (units held per SKU), `status: ReservationStatus`, `expires_at: datetime`, `order_id: str | None`; enum `ReservationStatus` with members `ACTIVE`, `CONFIRMED`, `RELEASED`, `EXPIRED`.
+- `inventory.errors`: new `ReservationNotFound`, `ReservationExpired`, `InvalidReservationState`, `IdempotencyConflict` (all subclass `InventoryError`); reuse the existing errors where they fit.
+- Time comes only from the injected clock. There is no background job: expiry must take effect without anyone calling a sweep.
+
+Additions decided in the interview:
+- `InventoryService(repository, ledger, clock, reservation_ttl=timedelta(minutes=20))` —
+  optional keyword, default 20 minutes.
+- `InventoryService.reserved(sku, warehouse) -> int` — units held by live holds.
+
+## Rules
+
+Quantities per (SKU, warehouse):
+`available = max(0, on_hand - allocated - reserved)`, where `reserved` counts only
+**live** holds (status `ACTIVE` and `now < expires_at`). `allocated` is unchanged
+(PLACED orders only).
+
+### reserve
+- Validation as `place_order`: `UnknownWarehouse`, `UnknownSku`, `InvalidQuantity`;
+  empty `items` or empty key → an `InventoryError`. A rejected request holds nothing.
+- Idempotency (one global key namespace), checked after input validation and before stock:
+  - key seen, same warehouse and same *requested* items (order-insensitive) → return the
+    existing reservation in its current state; nothing new is held, `expires_at` unchanged.
+  - key seen, different warehouse or items → `IdempotencyConflict`, whatever the original's state.
+- **Partial hold:** each line holds `min(requested, available now)`. Lines with nothing
+  available are omitted from `items` (no zero entries). If no line can hold anything →
+  `InsufficientStock`, nothing is created and the key stays unused.
+- New reservation: `ACTIVE`, `expires_at = now + ttl`, `order_id = None`, id `RES-0001`, …
+
+### expiry
+- A hold is expired from `expires_at` on, inclusive (`now >= expires_at`). From that instant
+  its units are available again and `get_reservation` reports `EXPIRED`, with no sweep call.
+- `CONFIRMED` and `RELEASED` holds never become `EXPIRED`.
+
+### confirm_reservation
+| state     | result |
+|-----------|--------|
+| ACTIVE    | new PLACED order for exactly the held `items`, `placed_at = now`; reservation → CONFIRMED, `order_id` set. Held units become allocated (available unchanged). No stock re-check. |
+| CONFIRMED | return the same order; create nothing (also after `expires_at`). |
+| RELEASED  | `InvalidReservationState` |
+| EXPIRED   | `ReservationExpired` |
+
+### release_reservation
+| state     | result |
+|-----------|--------|
+| ACTIVE    | → RELEASED, units available again |
+| RELEASED  | no-op, return unchanged |
+| EXPIRED   | no-op, return unchanged (still EXPIRED) |
+| CONFIRMED | `InvalidReservationState` |
+
+Unknown id (confirm / release / get) → `ReservationNotFound`.
+
+### interaction with existing operations
+- `receive` and `adjust` are never blocked by holds. If a write-off leaves on-hand below
+  what is held, `available` shows 0 and the reservations stay as they are.
+- `place_order` stays all-or-nothing and can only take available stock (i.e. net of holds).
+
+## Acceptance criteria (each is a test in `tests/test_reservations.py`)
+- [ ] reserve holds stock: `available` drops, `on_hand` unchanged, `reserved` reports it.
+- [ ] reserve returns ACTIVE, `order_id is None`, `expires_at == now + 20 min`; ttl is configurable.
+- [ ] partial hold: line capped at available; line with 0 available omitted.
+- [ ] nothing available on any line → `InsufficientStock`, no reservation, key reusable.
+- [ ] invalid input (unknown warehouse / SKU, bad quantity, empty items, empty key) → error, nothing held even for valid lines.
+- [ ] `place_order` cannot take held units.
+- [ ] at exactly `expires_at` the hold is EXPIRED and its units available; one tick before, still ACTIVE.
+- [ ] confirm ACTIVE → PLACED order with held items; available unchanged; allocated up, reserved down.
+- [ ] confirm twice → same order, no new order (also after `expires_at`).
+- [ ] confirm EXPIRED → `ReservationExpired`; confirm RELEASED → `InvalidReservationState`.
+- [ ] release ACTIVE → RELEASED, units freed; release again → no-op; release EXPIRED → no-op EXPIRED.
+- [ ] release CONFIRMED → `InvalidReservationState`.
+- [ ] unknown reservation id → `ReservationNotFound` for get / confirm / release.
+- [ ] same key + same request → same reservation, no extra hold, `expires_at` unchanged, item order ignored.
+- [ ] same key + same request after partial hold → returns it (compares requested, not held).
+- [ ] same key + different items or warehouse → `IdempotencyConflict`, also when original is finished.
+- [ ] write-off below held → available 0, reservation still ACTIVE with its items; confirm still works.
+- [ ] `python3 -m pytest -q` exits 0.
+
+## Non-goals
+- Extending / renewing a hold; partial confirm or release; multi-warehouse holds; a sweep API.
+- A `reserved` column in `stock_report` (owner indifferent; left out to keep `StockRow` stable).
+
+## Scope limits
+- Touch only `src/inventory/{models,errors,repository,service,__init__}.py`, the new test
+  file, README concepts, GLOSSARY, ADRs. No new dependencies.
